                  <!DOCTYPE html>
        h2#doctype-shortcuts
          | Doctype Shortcuts
          a.header-anchor(href="#doctype-shortcuts" aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p There are shortcuts for commonly used doctypes:
        dl
          dt doctype html
          dd
            pre.cm-s-default
              code
                span.cm-meta <!DOCTYPE html>
          dt doctype xml
          dd
            pre.cm-s-default
              code
                span.cm-meta <?xml
                span.cm-meta version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
          dt doctype transitional
          dd
            pre.cm-s-default
              code
                span.cm-meta <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd">
          dt doctype strict
          dd
            pre.cm-s-default
              code
                span.cm-meta <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd">
          dt doctype frameset
          dd
            pre.cm-s-default
              code
                span.cm-meta <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Frameset//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-frameset.dtd">
          dt doctype 1.1
          dd
            pre.cm-s-default
              code
                span.cm-meta <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.1//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml11/DTD/xhtml11.dtd">
          dt doctype basic
          dd
            pre.cm-s-default
              code
                span.cm-meta <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML Basic 1.1//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml-basic/xhtml-basic11.dtd">
          dt doctype mobile
          dd
            pre.cm-s-default
              code
                span.cm-meta <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//WAPFORUM//DTD XHTML Mobile 1.2//EN" "http://www.openmobilealliance.org/tech/DTD/xhtml-mobile12.dtd">
          dt doctype plist
          dd
            pre.cm-s-default
              code
                span.cm-meta <!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
        h2#custom-doctypes
          | Custom Doctypes
          a.header-anchor(href="#custom-doctypes" aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p You can also use your own literal custom doctype:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive" data-index="1")
          div.row(data-reactroot data-reactid="1" data-react-checksum="1482066191")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  doctype html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML Basic 1.1//EN"
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly data-reactid="7").
                  <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML Basic 1.1//EN">
        h2#doctype-option
          | Doctype Option
          a.header-anchor(href="#doctype-option" aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p
          | In addition to being buffered in the output, a doctype in Pug can affect compilation in other ways. For example, whether self-closing tags end with
          code />
          | or
          code >
          | depends on whether HTML or XML is specified. The output of
          a(href="attributes.html#boolean-attributes") boolean attributes
          | may be affected as well.
        p
          | If, for whatever reason, it is not possible to use the
          code doctype
          | keyword (e.g., just rendering HTML fragments), but you would still like to specify the doctype of the template, you can do so via the
          a(href="../api/reference.html#options")
            code doctype
            | option
          | .
        pre.cm-s-default
          code
            span.cm-keyword var
            span.cm-def pug
            span.cm-operator =
            span.cm-variable require
            | (
            span.cm-string 'pug'
            | );
            span.cm-keyword var
            span.cm-def source
            span.cm-operator =
            span.cm-string 'img(src="foo.png")'
            | ;
            span.cm-variable pug
            | .
            span.cm-property render
            | (
            span.cm-variable source
            | );
            span.cm-comment // => '<img src="foo.png"/>'
            span.cm-variable pug
            | .
            span.cm-property render
            | (
            span.cm-variable source
            | , {
            span.cm-property doctype
            | :
            span.cm-string 'xml'
            | });
            span.cm-comment // => '<img src="foo.png"></img>'
            span.cm-variable pug
            | .
            span.cm-property render
            | (
            span.cm-variable source
            | , {
            span.cm-property doctype
            | :
            span.cm-string 'html'
            | });
            span.cm-comment // => '<img src="foo.png">'
